{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 23, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "In fair Nippon’s land where sun doth rise\nA journey long in verse I’ll devise\nFrom Tokyo’s towers to Kyoto’s grace\nThrough temples high and gardens fair of place\n\n**Day the First: The Eastern Crown**\nUpon thy flight to Narita’s gate\nThou shalt find thy way to Tokyo’s estate\nWhere neon lights like stars do gleam\nAnd streets alive with dreams that teem\n\nBegin at Shibuya’s famed cross\nWhere throngs do rush like waves from loss\nThen seek the Meiji Shrine’s quiet shade\nWhere ancient trees in sacred glade\nDo whisper tales of gods of old\nTheir secrets told in silence bold\n\nFeast upon sushi fresh and bright\nAt Tsukiji’s market in the light\nOr wander Ginza’s golden way\nWhere art and fashion blend and sway\n\n**Day the Second: The Imperial Seat**\nTake the Shinkansen swift and true\nTo Kyoto’s realm of ancient hue\nWhere emperors of old did tread\nAnd temples rise where gods are fed\n\nFirst let Asakusa’s Senso-ji\nWith its lantern red draw nigh\nThen cross the Sumida’s gentle flow\nTo Ueno’s park where cherry’s glow\n\nIn the evening gold the Gion’s streets\nWhere geisha glide on silent feet\nAnd lanterns hang like stars on high\nPainting dreams ‘gainst evening sky\n\n**Day the Third: The Path of Zen**\nTo Arashiyama’s bamboo grove\nWhere sunlight dances ‘twixt the leaves above\nThen to Kinkaku-ji’s gilded spire\nWhere heaven’s light doth kiss the mire\n\nPartake of kaiseki’s art\nA feast for tongue and eye and heart\nWhere courses come in artful guise\nLike edible and sweet surprise\n\n**Day the Fourth: The Castle’s Might**\nTo Nara’s ancient deer park fair\nWhere sacred beasts with gentle care\nDo bow their heads to thee who bring\nShika senbei crisp and spring\n\nThen to Himeji’s white crane fly\nA fortress strong ‘gainst time’s swift eye\nWhere samurai of yore did stand\nAnd guard this jewel of sea and land\n\n**Day the Fifth: